            <ArticleTitle>Cushing's syndrome associated with functional black adenoma of the adrenal cortex.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1410-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 35-year-old woman who had bone pain in the extremities was found to have Cushing's syndrome, for which she had adrenalectomy. Pathologic examination revealed a solitary black adenoma. Bone scan and roentgenograms showed regional osteoporosis of the extremities and avascular necrosis of the hip. Her cushingoid manifestations and bone pain resolved after adrenalectomy and vitamin D therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
